<http://fdp.dcc.sib.swiss/catalog/b11dbf20-e08e-5bf1-a1e5-ba64457e17c0> a dcat:Catalog,
        dcat:Resource ;
    rdfs:label "Cohort demonstrator: Full integration of a national cohort into the SPHN infrastructure" ;
    ns4:applicableLegislation <https://www.fedlex.admin.ch/eli/cc/2007/279/de>,
        <https://www.fedlex.admin.ch/eli/cc/2013/617/de>,
        <https://www.fedlex.admin.ch/eli/cc/2013/642/de>,
        <https://www.fedlex.admin.ch/eli/cc/2022/491/de>,
        "Cantonal data protection laws" ;
    dcterms:abstract "The Cohort Demonstrator project facilitates the secure and efficient transfer of routine clinical data from multiple University Hospital Clinical Data Warehouses (CDWHs) to the Swiss Transplant Cohort Study (STCS).  To facilitate patient selection and linkage, the project implemented dedicated tools (IDEAL) for managing study participants. IDEAL (and Horus, at CHUV) supports the identification and secure linking of patient identifiers between the study and the hospital, ensuring compliance with data protection requirements and enabling seamless downstream data transfer. A key outcome of the project is the development of the Cohort Hospital Integration Layer (CHIL). CHIL ingests multisite RDF data using consistent terminology across hospitals and provides a user-friendly interface for querying study-specific datasets. This data is then integrated into the STCS research database, enhancing the data granularity, completeness, and usability of STCS data, unlocking new possibilities for real-world data analyses, AI-based research, and embedded sub-studies. This project also highlights the need for harmonised procedures and infrastructure across institutions to support sustainable data sharing practices. The solutions developed are designed to be reusable and adaptable, offering a blueprint for other cohorts and research initiatives aiming to harness routine clinical data across institutional boundaries." ;
    dcterms:accessRights <http://fdp.dcc.sib.swiss/catalog/b11dbf20-e08e-5bf1-a1e5-ba64457e17c0#accessRights> ;
    dcterms:conformsTo <http://fdp.dcc.sib.swiss/profile/a0949e72-4466-4d53-8900-9436d1049a4b>,
        <https://www.biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn/2024/2> ;
    dcterms:identifier "http://fdp.dcc.sib.swiss/catalog/b11dbf20-e08e-5bf1-a1e5-ba64457e17c0" ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://fdp.dcc.sib.swiss> ;
    dcterms:issued "2026-03-03T17:17:45.418303+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
